  '花山': { n: 'Kazan', tip: ['Emperor Kazan', '65th emperor', 'Lived: 968–1008', 'Reign: 984–986', 'Note: Tricked by Fujiwara no Kaneie and others into becoming a monk and giving up the throne (the Kanna Incident)'] },
  // 47.html（恵慶法師）
  '安法': { n: 'Anpō', tip: ['Priest Anpō', 'Family: Sixth son of Minamoto no 適 (reading of the name unknown); great-grandson of Minamoto no Tōru', "Note: Became a monk and lived in the Kawara-in, the mansion built by his great-grandfather Tōru. He was friends with many poets, such as Minamoto no Shitagō, Kiyohara no Motosuke, Taira no Kanemori, and Egyō"] },
  '恵慶': { n: 'Egyō', tip: ['Priest Egyō', 'Hyakunin Isshu: Poet of Poem 47, "Yaemugura..."', 'Note: His family and career are unknown. He was close to Anpō, and is said to have been friends with Ōnakatomi no Yoshinobu, Ki no Tokibumi, Kiyohara no Motosuke, and others'] },
  // 48.html（源重之）
